Z||000000||N_Man||09-02-2000||08:23 PM||||My car still isnt running quite right. even after an engine rebuild (its fully broken in) and what i believe to be a full set of tune up items.<P>I have replaced the following:<BR>Air filter  K&N<BR>fuel filter<BR>distributer cap & roter<BR>plug wires <BR>plugs   Bosch platinums<BR>PCV valve<BR>oil & filter<BR>ignition coil  MSD<BR>unplugged tach filter(seems to run better)<P>The car just feels to slow (it is slower than a friends stock GT) and i have a couple of performance goodies.<P>But as far as tune up items what may I be missing?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick's Dad||09-02-2000||08:57 PM||||How's your cat?<P>A clogged cat (The material inside breks up and jams the outlet) won't let your engine breath out, and will only make things worse. Jack the rear your car up and support it with jack stands (or back up onto some ramps), and, when things are cool to the touch, knock on the cat. It should have a solid, if slightly hollow, sound to it. If it sounds like there's steel wool rustling in it, replace it (Or can it, if you think that your car runs clean enough). I replaced my bad unit with a hi flow one from IRM (About $200 five years ago) along with the rest of the exhaust, and what a difference.<P>The IRM race system comes sans muffler, but I ran it on the street for years with no trouble, that is, until the Hooker tips that came with it rotted off.... The cat's still in good cond., tho....<P>------------------<BR>This should work until my site comes online....   <IMG SRC="http://homestead.deja.com/user.rshuman/files/Tmh.jpg"> ||||reg||1
